* Jenkins security
** Threat model
*** Credentials of every target system
*** Code execution on controller and agents
*** Supply chain: artifacts it builds and signs
** Security model
*** Realm = who you are
*** Authorization strategy = what you may do
*** Overall/Administer = full compromise
*** Builds run as SYSTEM by default
** Isolation
*** 0 executors on the built-in node
*** Agent-to-controller access control
*** Ephemeral agents for untrusted builds
** Groovy
*** Script Console = RCE by design
*** Sandbox and script approval
*** Trusted libraries run unsandboxed
** Secrets
*** secrets/master.key unencrypted on disk
*** Masking stops accidents only
*** Single quotes, not GStrings
** Web and network
*** CSRF crumbs, CSP, resource root URL
*** CLI and API tokens
*** CVE-2024-23897 file read to RCE
** Advisories 2017-2026
*** 1,541 issues, 88% in plugins
*** Permission checks, secrets, CSRF, XSS
*** 38% of plugin issues unfixed at publication
** Hardening
*** Patch core and plugins
*** Least privilege, folder credentials
*** jenkins.io infra as a reference
@endmindmap
